#: ../../../developer/general/website-style-guide.rst:3
#: 37ce2441de054b24b1cd9b20e5f97d99
msgid "Website style guide"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/general/website-style-guide.rst:6
#: c674d92e8db7423899306f62eab8fe3a
msgid ""
"This page explains the standards we follow for building and maintaining the "
"website. Please follow these guidelines and conventions when modifying the "
"website. For the standards governing the documentation in particular, please "
"see the :doc:`documentation style guide </developer/general/rst-"
"documentation-style-guide>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/general/website-style-guide.rst:10
#: b27f0ecb5d9d4446a744de456ef982bc
msgid "Coding conventions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/general/website-style-guide.rst:12
#: 5845dfba7f0d48a88432342816a7904a
msgid ""
"The following conventions apply to the website as a whole, including "
"everything written in HTML, CSS, YAML, and Liquid. These conventions are "
"intended to keep the codebase consistent when multiple collaborators are "
"working on it. They should be understood as a practical set of rules for "
"maintaining order in this specific codebase rather than as a statement of "
"what is objectively right or good."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/general/website-style-guide.rst:15
#: de5730e5c59e4559aecc86e3410618fa
msgid "General practices"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/general/website-style-guide.rst:18
#: 9596e9f669724eb2b8de8945ef60f3a8
msgid ""
"Use comments to indicate the purposes of different blocks of code. This "
"makes the file easier to understand and navigate."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/general/website-style-guide.rst:20
#: e76276bdd524441b8fe691deab4442d9
msgid ""
"Use descriptive variable names. Never use one or two letter variable names. "
"Avoid obscure abbreviations and made-up words."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/general/website-style-guide.rst:22
#: f421d144bc20439c834008ce63bb01d1
msgid ""
"In general, make it easy for others to read your code. Your future self will "
"thank you, and so will your collaborators!"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/general/website-style-guide.rst:24
#: a016632e6c744f91a13f824d5cc5d58e
msgid ""
"`Don’t Repeat Yourself (DRY)! <https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/"
"Don%27t_repeat_yourself>`__ Instead of repeating the same block of code "
"multiple times, abstract it out into a separate file and ``include`` that "
"file where you need it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/general/website-style-guide.rst:27
#: bfd2624aea114f88918ae4aa3ec268c1
msgid "Whitespace"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/general/website-style-guide.rst:29
#: adde8aa790304e9dbbd86553f517de3e
msgid "Always use spaces. Never use tabs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/general/website-style-guide.rst:30
#: 7e8d9cc088f84d4b906fb5eed20e6f23
msgid "Each indentation step should be exactly two (2) spaces."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/general/website-style-guide.rst:31
#: ca6b76675b3d43759002c31663d27113
msgid ""
"Whenever you add an opening tag, indent the following line. (Exception: If "
"you open and close the tag on the same line, do not indent the following "
"line.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/general/website-style-guide.rst:32
#: ef9690d54ac34954a0f68f9a601a09e1
msgid "Indent Liquid the same way as HTML."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/general/website-style-guide.rst:33
#: 19454abde986463e829448a293214f9f
msgid ""
"In general, the starting columns of every adjacent pair of lines should be "
"no more than two spaces apart (example below)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/general/website-style-guide.rst:34
#: d2c994260cc14c9484e2d1b0eab4b7c7
msgid ""
"No blank or empty lines. (Hint: When you feel you need one, add a comment on "
"that line instead.)"
msgstr ""

